<%# Backwards-compatible wrapper around Strata::Tasks::ShowComponent.
    Existing call sites using `render template: 'strata/tasks/show', locals: {...}`
    continue to work. New code should prefer `render Strata::Tasks::ShowComponent.new(...)`.

    Required locals:
    - task: Strata::Task - The task object
    - One of:
      - task_info: Array - An array of {label:, value:} hashes rendered as the info row.
      - assigned_user_display_text: String - Name of the assignee. Used in the default
        task_info row (status / due / assignee) that is rendered when no task_info: local
        is provided.

    Optional locals:
    - task_details_partial: String - Partial path to render for the task details. If not
      provided, the view looks for a partial named after the task type within `details/`.
    - breadcrumbs: Array - Array of {text:, link:} hashes overriding the default trail.

    Legacy content_for overrides:
    - :breadcrumbs - Previously, content_for(:breadcrumbs) would allow rendering custom
      breadcrumb markup. This has been removed; use the 'with_breadcrumbs_content' slot instead.
    - :task_info - Previously, content_for(:task_info) would allow rendering custom
      markup in the task info section. This has been replaced with the 'with_task_info_content' slot.
    - :task_details_partial - Previously, content_for(:task_details_partial) would allow rendering custom
      markup instead of the task details partial rendering. This has been replaced with the 'with_task_details_content' slot.

%>
<%= render Strata::Tasks::ShowComponent.new(
      task: task,
      assigned_user_display_text: local_assigns[:assigned_user_display_text],
      task_info: local_assigns[:task_info],
      breadcrumbs: local_assigns[:breadcrumbs],
      task_details_partial: local_assigns[:task_details_partial],
      details_locals: local_assigns.to_h
    ) %>
